1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,400
In this video we'll be going over the architecture of BurpSuite Enterprise Edition,

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,120
its core components and the connections between them.

3
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:17,000
Firstly we have the Enterprise server which is the main application server. It coordinates

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,600
between the other components. The Enterprise server is always installed on the same machine

5
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:29,720
as the web server. The web server provides the interface to users either via the web UI or one

6
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:38,080
of the APIs. Again the web server is always installed on the same machine as the Enterprise server.

7
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:43,400
Next we'll have one or more scanning machines. On standard deployments scans run on a scanning

8
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:49,780
machine. Think of these as your automated penetration testers. You can embed the scanning machine

9
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:55,620
on the same machine as the other components or you can deploy multiple external machines

10
00:00:55,620 --> 00:01:02,580
on which your scans can run. Scanning machines can then be grouped into scanning pools to

11
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:10,800
allow finer control over scanning resource. For Kubernetes deployments you don't have to

12
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:15,840
set up and manage individual scanning machines. Instead the system automatically creates additional

13
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:21,880
resource to cope with the number of concurrent scans that you need to run at any given time.

14
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:25,880
These resources are then scaled back down once they are no longer required.

15
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:32,740
All of these components will connect to some form of SQL database. This is to store data

16
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:38,900
about configured sites and scans, the results of scans and other configuration information.

17
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:43,780
You can use one of the following options. A bundled H2 database that can be installed on

18
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:50,220
the same machine as the Enterprise server and Web server. This option is suitable for a trial

19
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:59,420
or evaluation. For production deployments we recommend that you use your own external database.

20
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:04,160
This option lets you utilise any existing database infrastructure that you have, including database

21
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:09,920
backups and is more appropriate for larger deployments. For information about specific database

22
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:15,040
types and versions that are supported, please refer to our documentation database specification.

23
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:22,240
Note that you can start out using the bundled database and migrate to an external one later if

24
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:27,840
necessary. We recommend this approach in order to simplify the initial installation and evaluation process.

25
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:35,680
Finally are the Burps with Enterprise Edition services. Either three or four services on your machine,

26
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:40,880
depending on whether you are using the bundled database or not. For more information on services,

27
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:54,960
please refer to the Burps with Enterprise Edition services documentation. Thank you.

